NOTICE
======

Two of the skill documents in this repository (`git-release-hygiene` and
`github-repository-presentation`) began as documents contributed to the
`dsh-agent-team-presets` project (MIT, https://github.com/bloodarea/dsh-agent-team-presets).
The versions here include later revisions made in that project and local edits by
this repository's owner.

`skills/skill-creator/` is adapted from Anthropic's skill-creator, distributed under
the Apache License 2.0. The original license text ships unmodified as
`skills/skill-creator/LICENSE.txt`. The adaptation rewrites the guidance for DeepSeek
Harness (skill discovery, single-file format, invocation frontmatter), drops the
bundled `.skill` packaging step that DSH does not have, and replaces the
PyYAML-dependent validator with a zero-dependency one.

`academic-writing-suite` draws on two upstream works. Its de-AI prose rules are adapted
from `kipozannaki/Reduce-AI-Text` (MIT, https://github.com/kipozannaki/Reduce-AI-Text);
the upstream's self-evolving example library and multi-agent install machinery were
dropped, leaving only the rewriting rules. Its "write the introduction twice" sequencing
and its mechanical style gate (em-dashes, antithesis, intensifiers, throat-clearing,
hedging, passive voice) are adapted from `snl-ucsb/paper-writing-skill` (MIT,
https://github.com/snl-ucsb/paper-writing-skill); the upstream lab's voice profile and
LaTeX-specific tooling were not carried over. Its change-impact classes (A/B/C/D) are
adapted from `WenyuChiou/academic-writing-skills` (MIT,
https://github.com/WenyuChiou/academic-writing-skills). No third-party files are
redistributed here; the wording is rewritten for DeepSeek Harness and merged into one
document.

`figure-legend` is original to this repository, informed by the caption conventions in
`Yuan1z0825/nature-skills` (Apache-2.0), which is read as methodology only; no upstream
files are redistributed.

`paper-figure-audit` is original to this repository.
`intent-alignment` is original to this repository.

